an (R+5)", "Prediction markets price Acton around 68-69%"], "rationale": "October polling from high-quality pollsters (SSRS, Siena, YouGov, Suffolk) shows Acton leading by 4-8 points, and markets price her near 68%. Ramaswamy's $30 million cash on hand and Ohio's Republican fundamentals temper the edge, leaving a modest Democratic advantage.", "watch": "Ramaswamy's late advertising blitz funded by his own money could close the polling gap in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pits Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy, with term-limited Mike DeWine leaving the office. Polling through early October shows Acton ahead, with recent surveys from SSRS, Suffolk, and Marist giving her leads of 6 to 9 points, while a Republican-sponsored poll found a one-point Ramaswamy edge. Averages put her up roughly 5 points.\n\nRamaswamy has heavily outspent Acton, adding another $5 million of his own money in October and holding a large cash advantage. The campaign has turned sharply negative, and Ohio's Republican-leaning electorate keeps the race within reach for him. Markets and most forecasters still favor Acton, but the margin is modest enough that a late shift could decide the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6672, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6954, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.